10495 Chris Notes

- We often need user and practitioner data but sometimes only update/fetch one or the other
- We have disassociateUserFromCase, but index-user-on-case does not seems to have any mechanism to deal with such users? deleteUserRecord has the same issue.
- by separating user records across tables, we introduce the potential for data integrity issues (user table updated but not practitioners table, for instance)
- There are a ton of persistence functions. This is dangerous when they are not clearly differentiated.
- In associateUserWithCase and updatePractitioner, we do an update, but any undefined fields will not be updated. Is this a problem? (E.g., representing might be undefined?)
